OL,3,GNEWSA'Looking after my brother changed
OL,4,Achildhood for us'
OL,5,
OL,6,FSixteen-year-old Leah helps care for
OL,7,Fher younger brother Ben every day, but
OL,8,Ffor a long time she never thought of
OL,9,Fherself as a young carer.
OL,11,FBen, from Cheltenham, has a rare
OL,12,Fgenetic condition called Primary
OL,13,FCiliary Dyskinesia (PCD), which leaves
OL,14,Fhim vulnerable to infections and means
OL,15,Fhe needs intensive physiotherapy
OL,16,Fseveral times a day. Leah and her
OL,17,Fsiblings, Holly and Tom, help support
OL,18,Fhim with those treatments at home.
OL,23,APub: 12-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
